$NetBSD$

rtw89 -- Realtek 802.11ax driver, RTL8851BU subset for the NetBSD
native port (rtw89u).

Imported from the lab's FreeBSD snapshot at
os/freebsd/src/sys/contrib/dev/rtw89 (initial import based on
linux.git 028ef9c96e96, tag v7.0; lab commit 7ffebcdb702d).  The
snapshot already carries the lab fix RTW8851B_FW_FORMAT_MAX=1
(rtw8851b.c:29) so fw loading tries rtw8851b_fw-1.bin (format 1,
with element segments) first, matching the Linux ground truth.

License: every file is dual-licensed "GPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause"
(SPX-DX header in each file), so a native import under
sys/external/bsd is permitted, same as the rtw88 precedent.

Included (23 .c): core chan mac80211 mac mac_be phy phy_be fw cam
efuse efuse_be regd sar coex ps ser util debug + rtw8851b{,_rfk,
_rfk_table,_table,_bu}.  mac_be/phy_be/efuse_be are the BE-gen
shared layers required by RTL8851B.

Excluded: pci*/acpi/wow .c files, all rtw8852*/rtw8922* chips and
their tables, and the Linux-URB-based usb.c (the NetBSD usbdi
transport lives in sys/dev/usb/rtw89_usb.c, translated from the
FreeBSD native transport).  Headers pci.h/acpi.h/wow.h are kept:
they are in the include closure of core.h and only define types.

The .c file names carry an rtw89_ prefix (rtw89_core.c etc.): NetBSD
kernel objects are named by basename in the compile directory, and the
rtw88 lane in the same kernel would otherwise overwrite core.o, mac.o,
fw.o, coex.o ...  Contents are untouched; header names are unchanged
(the sources' quoted includes still resolve).

The `#if defined(__FreeBSD__)` blocks from the FreeBSD snapshot are
left in place verbatim: they compile out on NetBSD (which never
defines __FreeBSD__), and the guarded Linux-side code is exactly
what we want.  RTW89_LAB_* blocks are likewise inert (never defined
here).  The dist code is otherwise unmodified and must stay so --
NetBSD glue lives in ../netbsd.
